       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.          TRPTREQ2.
       AUTHOR.              C.I.HILLES/JIM COFFMAN (MAINTAINER).
       DATE-WRITTEN.        6/10/88.
       DATE-COMPILED.
      *INSTALLATION.        GOODYEAR TIRE AND RUBBER - AKRON.
      *SECURITY.
      *REMARKS.
      *
      *D   THIS IS A REPORT OF ALL REQUISITIONS ON THE SYSTEM.  THE USER
      *D   CAN HAVE MANY SELECT AND SORT OPTIONS.  THIS REPORT WILL BE
      *D   USED PRIMARILY TO ASSIST IN WEEKLY BUDGET REPORTING: THE
      *D   USER WILL ASK FOR ALL REQUISITIONS FOR THAT WEEK, SORTED
      *D   BY DEPARTMENT, FOR ALL DEPARTMENTS WITHIN A SPECIFIC
      *D   BUSINESS CENTER.

      *C  JUNE 23, 1994   CR KALMAN
      *C   ADDED CALL TO COBOL ERROR HANDLER -MCXCBLERR.
      *C
      *C  SEPT 10, 1996   CA YODER
      *C   MODIFIED PROGRAM FOR CENTURY DATABASE CHANGES.
      *C
      *C  DEC 18, 1996    CA YODER   REQ #95-023
      *C   ADDED ORIGINATOR AS A RESTRICT ITEM.  NOW THE REPORT
      *C   CAN PRINT SELECTED REQS BY ORIGINATOR INSTEAD OF HAVING
      *C   TO PRINT A RANGE OF ORIGINATORS.
      *C
      *C  23APR1997       DAVE PLUM
      *C   REVISED LOGIC IN PARAGRAPH 6010-SERIAL-LOOP TO MOVE ZEROS
      *C   TO NUMERIC FIELDS WITHIN BUF-DREQITM WHEN NO DREQITM RECORD
      *C   IS FOUND FOR A SPECIFIC MREQ REQUISITION NUMBER.  THE
      *C   PREVIOUS LOGIC ONLY MOVED SPACES TO THE ENTIRE BUFFER WHICH
      *C   LED TO DATA DECIMAL ERRORS WHEN THE NUMERIC FIELDS WERE LATER
      *C   MOVED TO SORT FIELDS.
      *C
      *C  09/03/1997      CA YODER
      *C   CORRECTED THE WAY THE INVOICE REPORT OPTION DISPLAYS UNIT
      *C   AND TOTAL COST.  PREVIOUSLY, THE UNIT COST OF EACH INVOICE
      *C   WAS ADDED TO DERIVE THE UNIT COST FIELD.  THEN, THE QUANTITY
      *C   WAS MULTIPLIED BY UNIT COST TO GET TOTAL COST.  THIS IS
      *C   INACCURATE BECAUSE MULTIPLE INVOICES WOULD GIVE A MEANINGLESS
      *C   UNIT COST.  NOW, THE UNIT COST IS CALCULATED BY DIVIDING TOTAL
      *C   INVOICE COST BY TOTAL INVOICE QUANTITY.  ALSO, A PROBLEM WITH
      *C   READING THROUGH INVOICE ITEMS WAS CORRECTED.  THE PROGRAM
      *C   READ ITEMS UNTIL THE REQ ITEM NUMBER WAS GREATER THAN INVOICE
      *C   ITEM NUMBER WHEN THE CONDITION SHOULD HAVE BEEN REVERSED.
      *C
      *C  11/14/1997      CA YODER     J THOMAS REQUEST
      *C   REMOVED THE "ON PO" OPTION FOR THIS REPORT.  IT WAS CAUSING
      *C   VERY LARGE REPORTS TO BE GENERATED, AND JIM SAID THE USERS
      *C   SHOULD NOT NEED TO USE THIS OPTION ANYWAYS.
      *C  01/27/1998      CA YODER
      *C   UN-COMMENTED THE ABOVE CHANGE.  SOME REQS WERE BEING SKIPPED
      *C   BECAUSE THEY WERE ON PO'S.
      *C
      *C  04/08/2004      CA YODER
      *C   ADDED OPTION TO INCLUDE REQS IN ARIBA BUYER (STATUS = "AR")
      *C   ONLY.
      *C

       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
       CONFIGURATION SECTION.
       SOURCE-COMPUTER.  AS400.
       OBJECT-COMPUTER.  AS400.
       SPECIAL-NAMES.  C01 IS NEW-PAGE.

       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
